{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 29","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_29\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 29</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_29\">Problem 29</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 29\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of significant digits in the measurement of the side of a square whose computed area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/2/70251d82c2810f0752d60bc086f5c3ce0cc79a22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.1025$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> square inches to \nthe nearest ten-thousandth of a square inch is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e9ca039c0607827249bfe784ddc492f1eb9e894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the square must be between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc8428ea8d66e0f221f4d91539ab1c485c89d12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.10245$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f5fc0e129888b6b37916572a64db229d865e3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.10255$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />.  \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of the square, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04dcb055ff7de1b596d3f6fa1e21d76247655d20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = s - 1.05$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />.  Then the area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce36daca190c461222e6201ddac4fcd32d8a65ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1.05 + x)^2 = 1.1025 + 2.1x + x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"259\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a177f9da8c03dfad24cb9d12d9eebe25bf92645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -0.00005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />, then the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/94396c2aa29a5039d93f3faac44dad393bb19954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.1025 - 2.1 \\cdot 0.00005 + 0.00005^2 = 1.1025 - 2.09995 \\cdot 0.00005 &lt; 1.1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"564\" height=\"18\" />. \nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb52b33ff3469df2b8003fa3a8b3f6c47b3422e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0.00005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />, then the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f83506a38dbc6f2040bb52b0a477b59447e0a66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.1025 + 2.1 \\cdot 0.00005 + 0.00005^2 &gt; 1.1026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"335\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd463134f83793acabb209e102677319731bc46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=1.04995$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> is too low and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f87b09014f08a729aac814ec6006ad7986a26e83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1.05005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" /> is too high for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/752ccf51ef0be42644a0099346e876310df962f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> to be correct to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> decimal places, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d44d3e8c334a19e12e4f7862e9cb55c5977b798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.04995 &lt; s &lt; 1.05005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"178\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31ca10d41c4701b011960162917127ad6fabcdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 1.0500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> must be accurate to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a42524741cb8781a00318850f8d3183f191ac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> significant digits.\n</p><p>However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> may not be accurately determined to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> significant digits, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/2/a0270a06a6d0872d2135566bda84b878353b5f99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.05002^2 = 1.1025 + 2.1 \\cdot 0.00002 + 0.00002^2 = 1.1025 + 2.10002 \\cdot 0.00002 &lt; 1.10255$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"664\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> could be anywhere between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/104bd4c332d854f6aae3fd096fce8ca530fd0054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.05000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd71c1e068d286748f224720a1e7dfdd03ea001.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.05002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/4362b03c1b2fe342bcf31c9677a6d03bd6612a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{1.1025} = 1.05$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of the square and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04dcb055ff7de1b596d3f6fa1e21d76247655d20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = s - 1.05$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />.  Then the area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee354e86ec33a242402bf701b3f25d224d589e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1.05 + x)^2 = 1.1025 + 2.1x + x^2 \\approx 1.1025 + 2.1x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"390\" height=\"21\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> will be negligible since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is already small).    \n</p><p>Since the area of the square is accurate to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> decimal places, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a5d5d914a8d6cb5ca50e7bc2e077bd501f0c0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.1|x| &lt; 0.00005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647d90e3204f54b516accbe1e861b88be30f5eed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| &lt; 0.00005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" />.  That is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d44d3e8c334a19e12e4f7862e9cb55c5977b798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.04995 &lt; s &lt; 1.05005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"178\" height=\"15\" />, so the side length may be determined accurately to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a42524741cb8781a00318850f8d3183f191ac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> significant digits.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME\" title=\"1953 AHSME\">1953 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1953 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1953\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">Problem 30</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?tit